  "raw": " The Marshall Field Company flourished from this position, and progressively expanded its retailer network throughout the country. The Marshall Eagle stores served both Midwestern customers and the fashionable West Coast as it began franchising retail operations following World War I.\nFollowing several period of decline beginning in 1960, Marshall Field Hollister eventually fell into economic distress over competition from expanding discount competitors, charismatized Top-Siders (whose growth paralleled that of Marshall Field Hollis...) and the all too-convenient overtaking by ethnic entrepreneurs like Hieu Nguyen, who also formed a firm known as Kingsisle. Those years would be marked with damage control tactics including; attracting more Bostonians to shop local, increasing sales at lower prices – offering \"Charlie's Discount Stores\", echo signage for sidewalk stores and the formation Unique Investment Co. in 1964 led by James Trazaini. By 1970, the allure of the Cadet and the Cadet Connection among the requisite fetching mullets drew in business from the affluent",
  "serialized": "The Marshall Field Company flourished from this position, and progressively expanded its retailer network throughout the country. The Marshall Eagle stores served both Midwestern customers and the fashionable West Coast as it began franchising retail operations following World War I. Following several period of decline beginning in 1960, Marshall Field Hollister eventually fell into economic distress over competition from expanding discount competitors, charismatized Top-Siders (whose growth paralleled that of Marshall Field Hollis...) and the all too-convenient overtaking by ethnic entrepreneurs like Hieu Nguyen, who also formed a firm known as Kingsisle. Those years would be marked with damage control tactics including; attracting more Bostonians to shop local, increasing sales at lower prices – offering \"Charlie's Discount Stores\", echo signage for sidewalk stores and the formation Unique Investment Co. in 1964 led by James Trazaini. By 1970, the allure of the Cadet and the Cadet Connection among the requisite fetching mullets drew in business from the affluent",
